WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:05.270
- [Interviewer] All right, Amber.

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:06.180
- Hey.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:07.410
- [Interviewer] Welcome back again.

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:08.760
- Hi, thank you for having me.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.972
- [Interviewer] So you had
a rough ride this year.

00:00:10.972 --> 00:00:14.360
You got beaten up not long ago.

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:17.603
- [Amber] Yeah, I did.
A few months ago. Yeah.

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:20.610
Things have changed a lot.

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:22.960
You know, I have a couple of friends

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.680
that are saying to me,
what's wrong with you?

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:27.113
You're not the same.

00:00:28.295 --> 00:00:30.290
So I started thinking about that.

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:31.340
Like, what's wrong with me?

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:32.320
I'm not the same.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:34.999
So then I had to start asking
that frightful question,

00:00:34.999 --> 00:00:38.270
like, am I different
because of what happened?

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:40.298
Have I been different
since what happened to me?

00:00:40.298 --> 00:00:44.753
And they're like, yeah, you are.

00:00:44.753 --> 00:00:45.586
As matter of fact,

00:00:45.586 --> 00:00:47.973
it is, about when that
shit happened to you.

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:51.717
Man, I went to the police station,

00:00:51.717 --> 00:00:54.570
and I walked into the thing,

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:57.318
the beginning, the desk, I
used to call the desk cop,

00:00:57.318 --> 00:00:59.883
totally acted like I was bothering him.

00:01:00.838 --> 00:01:02.460
He was like, from the beginning,

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:03.790
when I said I'm here to make a report

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:05.130
because I was assaulted.

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:08.990
He was like, oh, here we go
with another one of these again,

00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:10.810
like it was, everything was a problem.

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:13.950
And I was hurting physically
and mentally, you know?

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:17.700
And I was like, wow, I didn't
got behind the door yet

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:20.483
and I'm already being treated like crap.

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:23.280
So I was waiting.

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:26.280
I think I waited about an hour and a half,

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:27.370
waiting for someone to talk to me

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:30.880
just to at least take down what happened,

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:32.763
the memory I did have of it left.

00:01:35.162 --> 00:01:37.105
An hour and a half, I went
back up there like, you know,

00:01:37.105 --> 00:01:38.470
hey what's up?

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:39.763
Oh, you're still here?

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:42.280
All right, let me see if there's
someone who can help you.

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:44.960
I said, no, it's okay.

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:46.579
Have a great day.

00:01:46.579 --> 00:01:50.238
I walked out, he said hey,
get your face looked at.

00:01:50.238 --> 00:01:51.513
And I start crying.

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:56.120
That's what they want,
get that face looked at.

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:02.820
And at night sometimes, when I go sleep,

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:04.240
that's the only thing I keep hearing.

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:05.840
Get that face looked at.

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:07.600
Like, I'm not a study
in beauty or anything.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:08.660
I'm not going to knock myself down,

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:10.290
but I'm not going to put myself up there,

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:11.669
like I'm, you know, the most
beautiful woman in the world.

00:02:11.669 --> 00:02:12.502
- [Interviewer] You're beautiful.

00:02:12.502 --> 00:02:14.185
But having the broken teeth and the scars,

00:02:14.185 --> 00:02:15.110
it's got to make it tough.

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:16.863
- The scars, the teeth,

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:22.710
the fact that I used to be
able to get, I say any guy,

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:26.240
but I used to not have a
problem with catching a date.

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:29.010
Now I'm begging with the beggars.

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:33.151
I've had to go way low on my price.

00:02:33.151 --> 00:02:36.073
I do all kinds of things
to try to hide my flaws.

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.600
Then now I'm just like this is what it is,

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:41.930
take it, yes or no, you know.

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:44.283
Take it if you want it. If not, thank you.

00:02:45.586 --> 00:02:47.586
It's really hard because I'm feeling it.

00:02:50.216 --> 00:02:53.460
It also makes people think
that you're a doormat.

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:56.080
That they can do anything to you

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:58.723
or that they can abuse you or assault you.

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:01.733
And I had someone tell me,

00:03:03.143 --> 00:03:05.920
you think that guy fucked your face up?

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:07.970
I'll your face up.

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:12.500
And I'm like, how much work you do to it?

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:13.963
Like, it was like,

00:03:15.342 --> 00:03:18.133
nine things I could find
that's wrong with it.

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:20.633
And that hurts.

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:26.165
However, a lot of people
had great comments,

00:03:26.165 --> 00:03:28.290
and words of encouragement,

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:30.740
show awesome compassion.

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:33.313
And I just want them to
see that I'm not dead.

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:37.373
I'm still here,

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:43.729
but I'm broken, without a doubt.

00:03:43.729 --> 00:03:47.800
However, woe is me, remember
I said that a long time ago?

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:49.453
I never signed up for this shit.

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:55.865
So sometimes I get my
dark moments and I'm like,

00:03:55.865 --> 00:03:57.840
I never signed up for this.

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.050
I never asked for all these problems.

00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:00.920
I never asked for

00:04:02.230 --> 00:04:04.380
any of the things that
have happened to me.

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:09.720
I just want to look out for my sister.

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:14.723
I just want to take care of her.

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:20.210
Never knew that making that decision

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:22.593
was going to make my whole life suck.

00:04:24.370 --> 00:04:26.050
- [Interviewer] Tell me about your sister.

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:28.313
She's wonderful. She's a Republican.

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:32.083
She has a business.

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:35.093
She's the polar opposite of me.

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:38.700
Completely opposite thinking of me.

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:40.283
I love her so much.

00:04:42.972 --> 00:04:45.820
And she hates me.

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:47.890
She's doesn't hate me
because she doesn't know me.

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:49.570
We weren't raised together.

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:53.433
She hates what I
represent, or the way I am.

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:57.370
So she turned Republican.

00:04:57.370 --> 00:05:00.240
She is against drugs.

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:02.973
She's against people on welfare services.

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:07.950
I call her, you think
I'm a waste of space.

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:11.133
And she says, no you're
not, but I'll be this

00:05:11.133 --> 00:05:14.370
as long as she has what she has.

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:17.738
Nice cars, you know,
she's the polar opposite.

00:05:17.738 --> 00:05:20.253
She's just, she's awesome.

00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:23.840
And, but damn, I didn't
think that, you know,

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:28.840
making that decision was
going to be so life changing.

00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:31.143
So I hate that shit.

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:34.973
To turn my mom into my family,

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:37.730
to seek for help,

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:39.530
to do it right,

00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:42.890
to make sure my sister
wasn't in that apartment

00:05:42.890 --> 00:05:45.060
with no lights, no gas, no food.

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:46.370
I mean, maybe I think of it,

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:50.260
like maybe I could have went
to this entity or this service

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:52.530
or maybe this relative,

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:54.426
or maybe I could go to my
dad's side of the family

00:05:54.426 --> 00:05:56.476
instead of my mom's. It's always what if?

00:05:57.810 --> 00:06:00.580
I really tried to put my chin
up and, you know, take it on.

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:04.450
They say, what makes you,

00:06:04.450 --> 00:06:07.457
like what makes you cry will
make you laugh, you know.

00:06:07.457 --> 00:06:09.630
And I can laugh with my sister.

00:06:09.630 --> 00:06:11.320
I love her so much.

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:12.190
It's okay.

00:06:12.190 --> 00:06:14.760
Maybe one day she'll come down
here and you can meet her.

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:16.225
She's awesome person.

00:06:16.225 --> 00:06:17.823
And I looked at her and I think of

00:06:17.823 --> 00:06:21.412
all the things I could have
been, I should be, but,

00:06:21.412 --> 00:06:24.700
and I still could be, but I don't want to.

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:26.910
I don't got it in me no more.

00:06:26.910 --> 00:06:29.040
I don't want to go to school.

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:29.873
I don't want to be seen.

00:06:29.873 --> 00:06:30.870
- [Interviewer] You
don't go to school now?

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:35.680
- Nothing. I'm doing nothing
but feeling sorry for myself.

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:37.369
And I know it's fresh.

00:06:37.369 --> 00:06:38.911
It just happen.

00:06:38.911 --> 00:06:42.220
But with everything going
on in the world right now,

00:06:42.220 --> 00:06:45.120
it's not the time to really
be feeling sorry for yourself.

00:06:48.575 --> 00:06:50.240
- [Interviewer] And you're still working?

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:51.157
I have to.

00:06:52.307 --> 00:06:57.307
But I do, I did see yesterday,
I saw an awesome commercial

00:06:58.470 --> 00:07:01.960
with one of the, I don't
know if I can say it,

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:02.793
Amazon dealer,

00:07:02.793 --> 00:07:04.770
and I want to try to get a job
with them for the holidays.

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:06.820
I know there's massive hiring.

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:08.586
Try at least,

00:07:08.586 --> 00:07:09.957
try something,

00:07:09.957 --> 00:07:12.480
but no, I'm not working.

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:15.360
I mean, I'm still working,
not going to school.

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:16.193
- [Interviewer] You've
been working the streets

00:07:16.193 --> 00:07:17.026
for how long?

00:07:18.190 --> 00:07:21.760
- Ten years, hard, heavy. Ten years.

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:22.593
- [Interviewer] And looking back,

00:07:22.593 --> 00:07:26.430
what do you think of that
decision that you made?

00:07:26.430 --> 00:07:29.903
- To work on the streets?
To be out here doing this?

00:07:32.540 --> 00:07:34.060
At first, it was the right thing to do.

00:07:34.060 --> 00:07:36.394
It fed me, it did everything for me,

00:07:36.394 --> 00:07:39.090
but I didn't know anything
about the business,

00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:41.100
or I didn't have no pimp.

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:43.970
I have one friend to turn
me out when I was a kid.

00:07:43.970 --> 00:07:48.350
And like I said, I'm
looking for my Richard Gere

00:07:48.350 --> 00:07:49.440
and I'm Julia Roberts.

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:52.349
So I've always on the
fairytale side of it.

00:07:52.349 --> 00:07:53.900
- [Interviewer] So do you
think girls are looking

00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:55.580
for some guy to save them?

00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:56.413
- A savior?

00:07:57.600 --> 00:08:00.270
Yes, this called captain (indistinct).

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:02.633
- [Interviewer] Yeah.
That's a common thing.

00:08:02.633 --> 00:08:06.261
- Yes. They might not
admit it but they are,

00:08:06.261 --> 00:08:08.710
because who wants to be doing this

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:10.130
when they're like 70 years old

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:11.330
60 years old?

00:08:11.330 --> 00:08:12.163
You want to find someone.

00:08:12.163 --> 00:08:14.187
I want to find somebody
who's going to be like

00:08:15.095 --> 00:08:16.900
my Richard Gere,

00:08:16.900 --> 00:08:19.360
and it's going to make
all my problems go away

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:21.930
and just help me make everything easier.

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:23.397
- [Interviewer] And from
the girl's perspective,

00:08:23.397 --> 00:08:25.518
is that a real relationship,

00:08:25.518 --> 00:08:28.598
or is it just an arrangement
that provides security

00:08:28.598 --> 00:08:31.083
and gives them what they need?

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:33.830
Or is it both?

00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:34.690
- It could be both.

00:08:34.690 --> 00:08:35.530
It could be all three.

00:08:35.530 --> 00:08:36.780
(indistinct) arrangement.

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:39.900
- [Interviewer] Yeah. It's
always this blurred line.

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:41.330
- Right, it's all three.

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:45.190
Me, I'm getting to the point where,

00:08:45.190 --> 00:08:48.720
I'll just like, I'll take anybody.

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:50.796
He could be old, he could be young,

00:08:50.796 --> 00:08:52.094
could be girl.

00:08:52.094 --> 00:08:54.854
- [Interviewer] You've
been in love before?

00:08:54.854 --> 00:08:59.087
- A lot, yeah. Currently, I
thought I was in love right now.

00:08:59.087 --> 00:09:00.890
I thought I was in love.

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:03.980
But I really don't know what love is.

00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:05.671
The examples I've had,

00:09:05.671 --> 00:09:07.423
have been poor examples.

00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:12.200
I know what the definition of the word is.

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:13.920
I believe that I'm in love,

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:15.427
but at the end of the day,

00:09:15.427 --> 00:09:18.523
love wouldn't do the
things that it does to me.

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:21.290
So I don't know. Maybe not.

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:24.710
- [Interviewer] Do you feel
like you love yourself?

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:26.423
- They sort of told me
that, like they said,

00:09:26.423 --> 00:09:28.752
you can't let me until you love yourself.

00:09:28.752 --> 00:09:31.110
And I'm like, what do you mean?
What is love yourself mean?

00:09:32.060 --> 00:09:33.540
What does that mean?

00:09:33.540 --> 00:09:34.633
- [Interviewer] To love
yourself means to be able to

00:09:34.633 --> 00:09:38.470
accept all the good things
that life has to offer.

00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:40.970
In a relationship, that
would mean to be able to

00:09:40.970 --> 00:09:44.673
accept a partner who is
kind, supportive, patient,

00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:48.500
someone who's fully
invested in helping you

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:50.473
to fulfill your dreams.

00:09:50.473 --> 00:09:53.393
- That's like that Cinderella story.

00:09:54.353 --> 00:09:56.020
- [Interviewer] Maybe from
the world you come from

00:09:56.020 --> 00:09:58.137
it seems like a Cinderella thing.

00:09:58.137 --> 00:10:00.804
- (indistinct).

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:05.240
- [Interviewer] It's almost
like love needs to be

00:10:05.240 --> 00:10:08.942
this almost impossible
situation where both partners

00:10:08.942 --> 00:10:13.040
believe they're lucky
to have the other person

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:14.933
in their lives at the same time.

00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:22.510
I need to believe that I'm
lucky to have you in my life,

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:25.716
and you need to secretly
believe that you're lucky

00:10:25.716 --> 00:10:29.470
that I'm in your life
and that has to co-exist.

00:10:29.470 --> 00:10:31.432
So when that's out of balance,

00:10:31.432 --> 00:10:35.760
one person gets bored and then,

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:37.960
yeah, it falls apart.

00:10:37.960 --> 00:10:39.720
And it's a constantly changing dynamic

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:43.680
where one person, you know, gets older,

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:46.240
one person gets depressed,

00:10:46.240 --> 00:10:49.363
- Right. No, I can't say,
I mean, I love myself.

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:51.450
I can say that.

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:53.271
I love myself enough to put on clothes.

00:10:53.271 --> 00:10:57.468
I love myself enough to strive,
work on living every day.

00:10:57.468 --> 00:10:59.880
That's the kind of love I have for myself.

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:00.972
I love myself enough to live,

00:11:00.972 --> 00:11:03.960
and that'd be the best
way, or the best life.

00:11:03.960 --> 00:11:07.090
But I think I love myself enough to live

00:11:07.090 --> 00:11:10.390
because I wake up every morning,
like, ooh, thank you, Lord.

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:11.310
Thank you for waking me up.

00:11:11.310 --> 00:11:14.425
Even if it's to deal
with the worst day ever.

00:11:14.425 --> 00:11:15.403
Thank you.

00:11:16.273 --> 00:11:17.520
'Cause my mom passed away in her sleep,

00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:20.160
so I hold on dear waking up.

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:22.720
I think that's why I don't like
to go to sleep much, either.

00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:24.470
You know, but hey, it's inevitable.

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:32.093
I don't know, things have changed.

00:11:32.093 --> 00:11:34.925
I didn't want to, next time you saw me,

00:11:34.925 --> 00:11:37.280
I'd be in a mental institution

00:11:37.280 --> 00:11:38.660
or missing an arm or a leg

00:11:38.660 --> 00:11:41.350
and not know what happened
in that gap of time.

00:11:41.350 --> 00:11:43.370
You know, I just want to stay relevant

00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:46.210
and stay, somebody out there cares

00:11:46.210 --> 00:11:48.480
because I've seen the number, you know.

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:50.580
- [Interviewer] Is this your lowest point?

00:11:52.810 --> 00:11:53.643
- Yep.

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:58.310
No. My lowest point was
when I lost my children.

00:11:58.310 --> 00:12:01.090
So this is right around there.

00:12:01.090 --> 00:12:02.356
They're fighting.

00:12:02.356 --> 00:12:03.189
- [Interviewer] And
you have how many kids?

00:12:03.189 --> 00:12:04.610
- I have four children.

00:12:04.610 --> 00:12:06.160
- [Interviewer] And they're with who now?

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:06.993
- Not really sure.

00:12:06.993 --> 00:12:09.312
I know that my oldest is with his dad

00:12:09.312 --> 00:12:13.620
and the last three are
hopefully they're all together

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:15.690
in a foster home together or something.

00:12:15.690 --> 00:12:16.960
'Cause I got twins.

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:19.032
Then a year later I had another baby,

00:12:19.032 --> 00:12:23.338
and they were all taken by the
state and me and my issues,

00:12:23.338 --> 00:12:26.793
I didn't, I messed my twins up.

00:12:27.660 --> 00:12:30.143
This thing, my children,
my twins, visiting them,

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:35.930
I gave them an anxiety
condition where they worry

00:12:35.930 --> 00:12:38.780
about if the parents they're
with is going to leave them.

